Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:18:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] 055 (3/5): gen_games kind = wasm, a game as an .aot

A manifest with kind = wasm names its .aot (for the ESP32-S3, from our pinned wamrc) and the .wasm it was made
from, each with its sha256, and the toolchain that made them; it has no sources, include, flags or app. Both
files are exported at the pin and checked against their hashes (a symbolic link, a missing file or a wrong hash
is refused), so a stage is checked as a clone is. Only the .aot is built in, and only with STU_WASM=1:
games.cmake embeds it (EMBED_FILES) with a generated WASM_GAME wrapper, games.h lists the game under
#ifdef STU_WASM, and games.mk and the host build never have it. tests/gen_games_test.sh gains the cases: a
native and a wasm game together, the outputs, games.h with and without STU_WASM, a stage without a clone, and
refusals (a wrong .aot or .wasm hash, sources on a wasm game, no toolchain, a hash that is not hex, a missing
.aot, an unknown kind). The staged-wasm case was red before the .wasm was exported and green after.

Written by arcade for soroban's gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
